# GhostCache environment variables
#
# GhostCache does NOT load .env files. It has no dotenv support and no
# third-party dependencies. A variable takes effect only when it is in the
# environment of the process that runs `python3.12 -m ghostcache ...`, for example:
#
#   export GHOSTCACHE_MODEL=gemma4:e2b-it-qat
#   python3.12 -m ghostcache serve --mode live
#
# To use a local .env file (which .gitignore already ignores), export it into
# your shell first:  set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# This is the ONLY environment variable the current code reads
# (ghostcache/providers.py).

# Optional. The Ollama model used by live mode and `evaluate --mode live`.
# Order of precedence: --model flag, then GHOSTCACHE_MODEL, then the built-in
# default gemma4:e2b-it-qat. The model must already be pulled in a local Ollama.
# Fixture mode ignores it.
GHOSTCACHE_MODEL=gemma4:e2b-it-qat

# These are NOT environment settings in the current code:
# - Port, mode, database path and report path are CLI flags:
#   --port, --mode, --database, --output
# - The Ollama URL is fixed in source to http://127.0.0.1:11434.
# - No Sentry, Render, Backboard, Browserbase, ElevenLabs or Entire
#   configuration exists yet. Add their variables here only in the same change
#   that adds working code for them. Never commit real secrets.
